// @run
// @log 1
// @log 1
// @log 1
// @log 1
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_z` (leading `_` marks it unused)
// `.slice` over an UNDECLARED list whose element has a nested object field matching a
// DECLARED union arm's layout — silent-class-inventory D227, filed as "D179's SECOND site".
//
// It was a second site, and #1972 needed a second bound check for it: the trap fired INSIDE
// `refListElemNameOfExpr`, which `refListSlotOfExpr` itself calls, so no caller-side guard —
// D179's included — could cover it. But the LOUD reject the two guards left behind has ONE
// root, not two: nothing interns the nested `{ c2: 1 }` shape, because `collectAnonShapes`
// denies an anonymous row to any literal `objVariantName` claims and that scan is global.
// Rescuing the nested literal makes every spelling below run at once; there is no second
// rung, and D179 and D227 are ONE landing on the current tree.
//
// The four reads are the four containers that reach the same shape: the bare index, the
// `.slice` view, a `.filter` bound to a local, and the un-annotated intermediate local. The
// discriminators are unchanged and still hold — `.map` instead of `.slice`, an added second
// ref list (`const pad: Other[] = [{ o: 1 }]`), deleting the two `type` lines, or declaring
// `Cir2` outside the union each change the program's fate on the pre-fix compiler.
type Cir2 = { c2: i32 }
type Shape2 = Cir2 | i32
const c = [{ r: { c2: 1 } }]
print(c[0].r.c2)
print(c.slice(0, 1)[0].r.c2)
const d = c.filter((_z) => true)
print(d[0].r.c2)
const e = c
print(e[0].r.c2)
